Crowns down" celebration has drawn criticism from a Borussia Dortmund fan club, reopening debate over faith, inclusion and religious messaging in football.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88f8269025894ca782f1efc82a72a937875f0cfba57f5559eaecfba60986e913</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal Youth Olympics in Dakar end on high note</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d9c23abfcfdee00cba2f3d775ff7767fce5ebf432c979461c91c59be1bafb8e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T04:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820--d8ec73fdda7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Enthusiastic crowds attended the games in Senegal, with China taking home the most gold medals. It's the first Olympic Games since Russia's war on Ukraine where Russian athletes can compete under their own flag.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA loses bid to block UEFA evidence gathering against Infantino</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53a49d7caa56f27eebf86e410c3effa8318175e3c6d7baaaa449c59345ca9ab3</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T00:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-loses-bid-to-block-uefa-evidence-gathering-against-infantino/a-79935807--1a1ba793a2d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-loses-bid-to-block-uefa-evidence-gathering-against-infantino/a-79935807?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A New York judge has dismissed soccer governing body FIFA's attempts to shield its president from investigation. Europe's UEFA is seeking evidence of wrongdoing by Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey: Russia threatens against Canada and Germany over exclusion from tournaments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed1523af7e6aae2b41a25fd13a0b1e571a77050c76395b930b67e027f6808ce2</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-russia-threatens-against-canada-and-germany-over-exclusion-from-tournaments/a-79942676--747c5baa6347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-russia-threatens-against-canada-and-germany-over-exclusion-from-tournaments/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fortnight after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8539a046af592025f58dea02da59c24afb210201ec578751465f5f0e69de1225</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's ice hockey team says Russia replacing it at World Juniors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:084452d2d2ec1ba44ec4d0ab013658b5dfa21ace8375390e03f13dcebbab99ee</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844--43300d3ba1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The wrangling over Russia's return to international ice hockey continues, with Norway saying it has been kicked out of the next major tournament to accommodate Russia. Switzerland has joined a "boycott."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany hopes to host world ice hockey championship — without Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07063d4a79eaf56095e5e63d2f274c9920a6966789e20ff42776158669a6324e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536--60661c53ebb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">International protests continue after a court ruled that Russia must be allowed to return to international ice hockey. Germany is seeking a solution that will allow the country to host next year's world championship.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about the IIHF Women's Ice Hockey World Championship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38af1a43d739d9a947c8f726150b400ed91f4471b98b2c7c4e1517fa306aca6d</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148--d773b0d8af6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As ice hockey's governing body continues to wrangle over how to respond to a CAS order to reinstate Russia to international play, the top women's tournament gets underway in Denmark without Russia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russia is back in world sport, but who is drug testing its athletes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:919eae9649440771979717b4469ca28c76958582b4812310c7ab2b65c5b5f98b</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467--6f0e1f90efa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e12041533f118678ca4d05050817fcf719e681990a0232ced084e5cc7c6a7199</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1237a22e8b81991e3b4407416c4a01bf87911c2bfdca6aac23d15fcb186dcb9</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
